{
  "$schema": "https://html-doc.dev/schema/page-v1.json",
  "kind": "page",
  "schema_version": 1,
  "title": "Primitives reference",
  "accent": "teal",
  "meta": {
    "eyebrow": "Reference",
    "subtitle": "Every Custom Element shipped with v2. Each entry: what it does, the JSON shape, every attribute, and a live example you can interact with.",
    "audience": "Author",
    "date": "2026-05-18",
    "read_time": "~12 min read",
    "order": 20,
    "summary": "Every primitive with JSON shape + live example.",
    "updated": "2026-05-18"
  },
  "blocks": [
    {
      "kind": "tldr",
      "summary": "17 primitives in v1. Inline kinds compose inside rich-text content arrays. Block kinds stand alone inside sections. Layout kinds wrap the page structurally.",
      "bullets": [
        "Inline (8): glossary-term, ext-ref, code, em, strong, link — and string literals which are also valid.",
        "Block (12): paragraph, heading, list, code, callout, insight, info-tip, kpi-grid, compare-grid, scope-grid, bar-chart, step-flow.",
        "Visual primitives (3): chart, diagram, live-snippet. SVG and JS-backed.",
        "Layout (4): page-chrome, page-nav, page-toc, page-cover. Set by your HTML stub, not the JSON."
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "section",
      "id": "inline",
      "title": "Inline kinds",
      "lead": "Used inside any richString — paragraph.content, list.items[*], callout.content, etc. Mix strings with these objects in an array.",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "heading",
          "level": 3,
          "id": "glossary-term",
          "title": "glossary-term"
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            "Hover for a tooltip with the definition; click to pin. Resolves the ",
            {
              "kind": "code",
              "text": "term"
            },
            " attribute against the active glossary domains in priority order. ",
            {
              "kind": "code",
              "text": "in"
            },
            " disambiguates when two domains use the same term. ",
            {
              "kind": "code",
              "text": "lang"
            },
            " overrides the project language for that instance."
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "code",
          "language": "json",
          "source": "{ \"kind\": \"glossary-term\", \"term\": \"ACID\", \"text\": \"ACID\" }\n{ \"kind\": \"glossary-term\", \"term\": \"ACID\", \"in\": \"chemistry\" }\n{ \"kind\": \"glossary-term\", \"term\": \"ACID\", \"lang\": \"tr\" }"
        },
        {
          "kind": "callout",
          "type": "neutral",
          "title": "Live",
          "content": [
            "Hover this term: ",
            {
              "kind": "glossary-term",
              "term": "ACID",
              "text": "ACID"
            },
            ". Then click it to pin. Move the mouse toward the tooltip — bridge-hover keeps it open so you can select the text or click the link."
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "heading",
          "level": 3,
          "id": "ext-ref",
          "title": "ext-ref"
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            "Like glossary-term but for external entities (tools, papers, people). Same hover-bridge-pin behavior. Reads from ",
            {
              "kind": "code",
              "text": "_kit/extrefs/<domain>.json"
            },
            " (or project kit.json overrides). Each entry has a ",
            {
              "kind": "code",
              "text": "summary"
            },
            " and a ",
            {
              "kind": "code",
              "text": "link"
            },
            "; the tooltip shows the name + summary, with a Learn more button to the link."
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "code",
          "language": "json",
          "source": "{ \"kind\": \"ext-ref\", \"name\": \"Pagefind\", \"text\": \"Pagefind\" }"
        },
        {
          "kind": "callout",
          "type": "neutral",
          "title": "Live",
          "content": [
            "Click this reference: ",
            {
              "kind": "ext-ref",
              "name": "Pagefind",
              "text": "Pagefind"
            },
            "."
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "heading",
          "level": 3,
          "id": "code-em-strong-link",
          "title": "code, em, strong, link"
        },
        {
          "kind": "code",
          "language": "json",
          "source": "{ \"kind\": \"code\",   \"text\": \"build_manifest()\" }\n{ \"kind\": \"em\",     \"text\": \"italic\" }\n{ \"kind\": \"strong\", \"text\": \"bold\" }\n{ \"kind\": \"link\",   \"text\": \"jsDelivr\", \"href\": \"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net\" }"
        },
        {
          "kind": "callout",
          "type": "neutral",
          "title": "Live",
          "content": [
            "Inline code: ",
            {
              "kind": "code",
              "text": "build_manifest()"
            },
            ". Italic ",
            {
              "kind": "em",
              "text": "for emphasis"
            },
            ". Bold ",
            {
              "kind": "strong",
              "text": "for impact"
            },
            ". External link: ",
            {
              "kind": "link",
              "text": "jsDelivr",
              "href": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net"
            },
            " — opens in a new tab with noopener."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "section",
      "id": "prose",
      "title": "Prose primitives",
      "lead": "paragraph, heading, list, code — the four building blocks of any prose section. Used together they cover ~80% of typical content.",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "heading",
          "level": 3,
          "id": "paragraph",
          "title": "paragraph"
        },
        {
          "kind": "code",
          "language": "json",
          "source": "{ \"kind\": \"paragraph\", \"content\": \"A plain string works for unadorned prose.\" }\n{ \"kind\": \"paragraph\", \"content\": [\n  \"Or an array mixing \",\n  { \"kind\": \"strong\", \"text\": \"inline nodes\" },\n  \" with strings.\"\n] }"
        },
        {
          "kind": "heading",
          "level": 3,
          "id": "heading",
          "title": "heading"
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            "Sub-headings inside a section. ",
            {
              "kind": "code",
              "text": "level"
            },
            " is 3 or 4 (h1 = page title, h2 = section title — both produced automatically). Optional ",
            {
              "kind": "code",
              "text": "id"
            },
            " for permalinks; auto-slugified if absent."
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "code",
          "language": "json",
          "source": "{ \"kind\": \"heading\", \"level\": 3, \"title\": \"Sub-heading\", \"id\": \"sub\" }\n{ \"kind\": \"heading\", \"level\": 4, \"title\": \"Sub-sub-heading\" }"
        },
        {
          "kind": "heading",
          "level": 3,
          "id": "list",
          "title": "list"
        },
        {
          "kind": "code",
          "language": "json",
          "source": "{ \"kind\": \"list\", \"style\": \"bullet\", \"items\": [\n  \"Plain string item.\",\n  [\"Or an array with \", { \"kind\": \"code\", \"text\": \"inline\" }, \" nodes.\"]\n] }\n{ \"kind\": \"list\", \"style\": \"numbered\", \"items\": [\"step 1\", \"step 2\"] }"
        },
        {
          "kind": "heading",
          "level": 3,
          "id": "code",
          "title": "code"
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            "Code blocks. ",
            { "kind": "code", "text": "language" },
            " is informational; the renderer puts a ",
            { "kind": "code", "text": "language-*" },
            " class on the inner ",
            { "kind": "code", "text": "<code>" },
            " so Prism (loaded lazily from CDN) highlights on demand. The runtime then adds a gray gutter with line numbers and — for brace languages — a click target on each foldable region's opening line."
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "code",
          "language": "json",
          "source": "{\n  \"kind\": \"code\",\n  \"language\": \"python\",\n  \"source\": \"def hello():\\n    print('world')\"\n}"
        },
        {
          "kind": "heading",
          "level": 3,
          "id": "annotated-code",
          "title": "annotated-code"
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "content": "Numbered code annotations. Markers like <code>(1)</code> / <code>(2)</code> inside the source become circular accent chips that pair with a numbered side panel. Hover or click any chip lights the matching row and vice versa. Prism highlights first so the chips survive the token tree."
        },
        {
          "kind": "code",
          "language": "json",
          "source": "{\n  \"kind\": \"annotated-code\",\n  \"language\": \"javascript\",\n  \"source\": \"const x = 1; // (1)\\nfunction greet(name) { // (2)\\n  return `Hello, ${name}!`;\\n}\",\n  \"annotations\": [\n    { \"id\": 1, \"content\": \"<code>const</code> creates a block-scoped binding.\" },\n    { \"id\": 2, \"content\": \"Functions are first-class values.\" }\n  ]\n}"
        },
        {
          "kind": "annotated-code",
          "language": "javascript",
          "source": "const x = 1; // (1)\nfunction greet(name) { // (2)\n  return `Hello, ${name}!`;\n}",
          "annotations": [
            { "id": 1, "content": "<code>const</code> creates a block-scoped binding." },
            { "id": 2, "content": "Functions are first-class values." }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "section",
      "id": "emphasis",
      "title": "Emphasis primitives",
      "lead": "callout, insight, info-tip — three ways to highlight content with different weight. Match weight to reader signal.",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "heading",
          "level": 3,
          "id": "callout",
          "title": "callout"
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            "Block-level themed note. ",
            {
              "kind": "code",
              "text": "type"
            },
            " is ",
            {
              "kind": "code",
              "text": "warn"
            },
            ", ",
            {
              "kind": "code",
              "text": "danger"
            },
            ", ",
            {
              "kind": "code",
              "text": "success"
            },
            ", or ",
            {
              "kind": "code",
              "text": "neutral"
            },
            " (default). Optional title. Content is richString."
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "code",
          "language": "json",
          "source": "{\n  \"kind\": \"callout\",\n  \"type\": \"warn\",\n  \"title\": \"Watch the lock\",\n  \"content\": \"Compaction holds a metadata lock; long jobs block writers.\"\n}"
        },
        {
          "kind": "callout",
          "type": "warn",
          "title": "warn",
          "content": "Yellow-bordered, used for caveats."
        },
        {
          "kind": "callout",
          "type": "danger",
          "title": "danger",
          "content": "Red-bordered, used for breaking changes or risks."
        },
        {
          "kind": "callout",
          "type": "success",
          "title": "success",
          "content": "Green-bordered, used for confirmations."
        },
        {
          "kind": "callout",
          "type": "neutral",
          "title": "neutral",
          "content": "Gray-bordered, used for general notes."
        },
        {
          "kind": "heading",
          "level": 3,
          "id": "insight",
          "title": "insight"
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "content": "A pull-quote for a key takeaway. Larger and more visually distinct than a paragraph — used to mark the one sentence per section worth slowing down for."
        },
        {
          "kind": "code",
          "language": "json",
          "source": "{ \"kind\": \"insight\", \"content\": \"The catalog is the locking primitive. Snapshots are the multi-version mechanism.\" }"
        },
        {
          "kind": "insight",
          "content": "The catalog is the locking primitive. Snapshots are the multi-version mechanism."
        },
        {
          "kind": "heading",
          "level": 3,
          "id": "info-tip",
          "title": "info-tip"
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            "Native ",
            {
              "kind": "code",
              "text": "<details>"
            },
            " in disguise — collapsed by default, expand on click. Use to defer optional depth without disrupting the skim path. ",
            {
              "kind": "code",
              "text": "content"
            },
            " accepts an array of content blocks (paragraphs, code, callouts, ..)."
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "code",
          "language": "json",
          "source": "{\n  \"kind\": \"info-tip\",\n  \"summary\": \"How the lock actually works\",\n  \"content\": [\n    { \"kind\": \"paragraph\", \"content\": \"Two writers race ...\" }\n  ]\n}"
        },
        {
          "kind": "info-tip",
          "summary": "Click to expand a live info-tip",
          "content": [
            {
              "kind": "paragraph",
              "content": "info-tip is the right primitive when the curious 5% of readers want the full story but the other 95% need to keep moving."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "section",
      "id": "layout",
      "title": "Structured-layout primitives",
      "lead": "tldr, kpi-grid, compare-grid, scope-grid, step-flow — when prose isn't the right shape.",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "heading",
          "level": 3,
          "id": "tldr",
          "title": "tldr"
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            "Top-level only. Highlighted opener box with optional ",
            {
              "kind": "code",
              "text": "title"
            },
            ", a ",
            {
              "kind": "code",
              "text": "summary"
            },
            " line, and ",
            {
              "kind": "code",
              "text": "bullets"
            },
            " — each bullet is rich-text."
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "code",
          "language": "json",
          "source": "{\n  \"kind\": \"tldr\",\n  \"summary\": \"One-sentence essence.\",\n  \"bullets\": [\n    \"Three to five concrete points.\",\n    \"Each bullet may include inline kinds like glossary terms.\"\n  ]\n}"
        },
        {
          "kind": "tldr",
          "title": "TL;DR (example)",
          "summary": "One-sentence essence. The summary line is bigger than bullets and reads first.",
          "bullets": [
            "Three to five concrete points.",
            "Each bullet may include inline kinds like glossary terms or links.",
            "Top-level placement is the canonical use; this one sits inline as a sample."
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "heading",
          "level": 3,
          "id": "kpi-grid",
          "title": "kpi-grid"
        },
        {
          "kind": "code",
          "language": "json",
          "source": "{\n  \"kind\": \"kpi-grid\",\n  \"tiles\": [\n    { \"num\": \"17\",   \"label\": \"Primitives\" },\n    { \"num\": \"JSON\", \"label\": \"Source\" },\n    { \"num\": \"0\",    \"label\": \"Build steps for content\" }\n  ]\n}"
        },
        {
          "kind": "kpi-grid",
          "tiles": [
            { "num": "17",   "label": "Primitives" },
            { "num": "JSON", "label": "Source" },
            { "num": "0",    "label": "Build steps for content" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "heading",
          "level": 3,
          "id": "table",
          "title": "table"
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "content": "First-class JSON table. Two shapes: flat <code>rows</code> or grouped <code>groups</code>. Renders into a real <code>&lt;table&gt;</code> plus a runtime control bar (filter input, stats counter, Table / List / Cards view toggle, sticky header, full-width auto-fit). Object-form headers and cells declare chip filters with multi-valued cells; groups are collapsible."
        },
        {
          "kind": "heading",
          "level": 4,
          "title": "Flat rows"
        },
        {
          "kind": "code",
          "language": "json",
          "source": "{\n  \"kind\": \"table\",\n  \"headers\": [\"Stage\", \"Status\", \"Duration\"],\n  \"rows\": [\n    [\"Plan\",  \"done\",         \"1d\"],\n    [\"Build\", \"done\",         \"3d\"],\n    [\"Test\",  \"in-progress\",  \"2d\"],\n    [\"Ship\",  \"queued\",       \"—\"]\n  ]\n}"
        },
        {
          "kind": "table",
          "headers": ["Stage", "Status", "Duration"],
          "rows": [
            ["Plan",  "done",        "1d"],
            ["Build", "done",        "3d"],
            ["Test",  "in-progress", "2d"],
            ["Ship",  "queued",      "—"]
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "heading",
          "level": 4,
          "title": "Grouped rows with per-group counts"
        },
        {
          "kind": "code",
          "language": "json",
          "source": "{\n  \"kind\": \"table\",\n  \"headers\": [\"Engine\", \"Storage\", \"License\"],\n  \"groups\": [\n    { \"title\": \"Lakehouse formats\",\n      \"rows\": [\n        [\"Apache Iceberg\", \"Object store\", \"Apache 2.0\"],\n        [\"Delta Lake\",    \"Object store\", \"Apache 2.0\"]\n      ]\n    },\n    { \"title\": \"Query engines\",\n      \"rows\": [[\"Trino\", \"Pluggable\", \"Apache 2.0\"]]\n    }\n  ]\n}"
        },
        {
          "kind": "table",
          "headers": ["Engine", "Storage", "License"],
          "groups": [
            { "title": "Lakehouse formats",
              "rows": [
                ["Apache Iceberg", "Object store", "Apache 2.0"],
                ["Apache Hudi",    "Object store", "Apache 2.0"],
                ["Delta Lake",     "Object store", "Apache 2.0"]
              ]
            },
            { "title": "Query engines",
              "rows": [
                ["Trino",  "Pluggable", "Apache 2.0"],
                ["Presto", "Pluggable", "Apache 2.0"]
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "heading",
          "level": 4,
          "title": "Chip filters + multi-valued cells"
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "content": "Headers can declare a fixed chip set with <code>filter: \"chips\"</code>; cells use the object form <code>{ value, values }</code> to belong to one or more chip values. AND across columns, OR within a column. Combine with the text filter."
        },
        {
          "kind": "code",
          "language": "json",
          "source": "{\n  \"kind\": \"table\",\n  \"headers\": [\n    \"Engine\",\n    { \"label\": \"Tags\", \"filter\": \"chips\",\n      \"values\": [\"lakehouse\", \"streaming\", \"query\"] },\n    { \"label\": \"Maturity\", \"filter\": \"chips\",\n      \"values\": [\"incubating\", \"ga\", \"experimental\"] }\n  ],\n  \"rows\": [\n    [\"Apache Iceberg\",\n      { \"values\": [\"lakehouse\"] },\n      { \"value\": \"GA\", \"values\": [\"ga\"] }],\n    [\"Apache Paimon\",\n      { \"values\": [\"lakehouse\", \"streaming\"] },\n      { \"value\": \"Incubating\", \"values\": [\"incubating\"] }],\n    [\"Trino\",\n      { \"values\": [\"query\"] },\n      { \"value\": \"GA\", \"values\": [\"ga\"] }]\n  ]\n}"
        },
        {
          "kind": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Engine",
            { "label": "Tags",     "filter": "chips", "values": ["lakehouse", "streaming", "query", "metadata"] },
            { "label": "Maturity", "filter": "chips", "values": ["incubating", "ga", "experimental"] }
          ],
          "rows": [
            ["Apache Iceberg",   { "values": ["lakehouse", "metadata"] },   { "value": "GA",           "values": ["ga"] }],
            ["Apache Hudi",      { "values": ["lakehouse", "streaming"] },  { "value": "GA",           "values": ["ga"] }],
            ["Delta Lake",       { "values": ["lakehouse"] },                { "value": "GA",           "values": ["ga"] }],
            ["Apache Paimon",    { "values": ["lakehouse", "streaming"] },  { "value": "Incubating",   "values": ["incubating"] }],
            ["Trino",            { "values": ["query"] },                    { "value": "GA",           "values": ["ga"] }],
            ["Apache Flink",     { "values": ["streaming"] },                { "value": "GA",           "values": ["ga"] }],
            ["Pulsar Functions", { "values": ["streaming", "metadata"] },   { "value": "Experimental", "values": ["experimental"] }]
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "heading",
          "level": 3,
          "id": "compare-grid",
          "title": "compare-grid"
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            "Side-by-side cards. ",
            {
              "kind": "code",
              "text": "verdict"
            },
            " is ",
            {
              "kind": "code",
              "text": "good"
            },
            ", ",
            {
              "kind": "code",
              "text": "bad"
            },
            ", or ",
            {
              "kind": "code",
              "text": "neutral"
            },
            " — sets the top-border color."
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "code",
          "language": "json",
          "source": "{\n  \"kind\": \"compare-grid\",\n  \"cards\": [\n    { \"verdict\": \"bad\",  \"title\": \"Before\", \"content\": \"...\" },\n    { \"verdict\": \"good\", \"title\": \"After\",  \"content\": \"...\" }\n  ]\n}"
        },
        {
          "kind": "compare-grid",
          "cards": [
            {
              "verdict": "bad",
              "title": "Authored HTML (v1)",
              "content": "Hand-written tags. Tree-edits via string ops. AI tooling brittle."
            },
            {
              "verdict": "good",
              "title": "Authored JSON (v2)",
              "content": "Structured tree. Atomic edits. JSON.parse is the contract."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "heading",
          "level": 3,
          "id": "scope-grid",
          "title": "scope-grid"
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            "Two columns with semantic borders. ",
            {
              "kind": "code",
              "text": "status"
            },
            " is ",
            {
              "kind": "code",
              "text": "in"
            },
            " (green top border) or ",
            {
              "kind": "code",
              "text": "out"
            },
            " (gray)."
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "code",
          "language": "json",
          "source": "{\n  \"kind\": \"scope-grid\",\n  \"columns\": [\n    { \"status\": \"in\",  \"title\": \"v1\",     \"items\": [\"...\"] },\n    { \"status\": \"out\", \"title\": \"Future\", \"items\": [\"...\"] }\n  ]\n}"
        },
        {
          "kind": "scope-grid",
          "columns": [
            {
              "status": "in",
              "title": "v2 ships",
              "items": [
                "JSON-source runtime rendering",
                "Multi-domain glossary with EN/TR",
                "Visual Viewport pinch-zoom fix",
                "Pagefind search on built sites"
              ]
            },
            {
              "status": "out",
              "title": "Out of scope",
              "items": [
                "Markdown authoring path",
                "Server-side rendering",
                "Per-user authentication",
                "Inline glossary editing UI"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "heading",
          "level": 3,
          "id": "step-flow",
          "title": "step-flow"
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "content": "Numbered cards for ordered actions, build steps, or migration paths."
        },
        {
          "kind": "code",
          "language": "json",
          "source": "{\n  \"kind\": \"step-flow\",\n  \"steps\": [\n    { \"num\": \"1\", \"title\": \"Init\",  \"meta\": \"~1 min\", \"content\": \"html-doc init\" },\n    { \"num\": \"2\", \"title\": \"Author\", \"content\": \"Write the JSON page.\" }\n  ]\n}"
        },
        {
          "kind": "step-flow",
          "steps": [
            {
              "num": "1",
              "title": "Init",
              "meta": "~1 min · one-time per project",
              "content": "html-doc init creates docs/_kit symlink."
            },
            {
              "num": "2",
              "title": "Author",
              "meta": "iterative",
              "content": "Write a JSON page and an HTML stub side by side; the renderer fetches the JSON at load time."
            },
            {
              "num": "3",
              "title": "Build",
              "meta": "before deploy or before sharing standalone",
              "content": "html-doc build → manifest, llms.txt, dist/site/, dist/standalone/, Pagefind index (if pagefind on PATH)."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "section",
      "id": "visual",
      "title": "Visual primitives",
      "lead": "bar-chart, chart, diagram, live-snippet — the rich content primitives that justify the JSON-source choice over Markdown.",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "heading",
          "level": 3,
          "id": "bar-chart",
          "title": "bar-chart"
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            "Row-per-item horizontal bars. Layout-safe by structure (no label collision). ",
            {
              "kind": "code",
              "text": "value"
            },
            " on each row; ",
            {
              "kind": "code",
              "text": "max"
            },
            " optional (defaults to ",
            {
              "kind": "code",
              "text": "max(rows.value)"
            },
            "); ",
            {
              "kind": "code",
              "text": "display"
            },
            " optional override for the readout text; ",
            {
              "kind": "code",
              "text": "color"
            },
            " is one of accent / warn / danger / success."
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "code",
          "language": "json",
          "source": "{\n  \"kind\": \"bar-chart\",\n  \"rows\": [\n    { \"label\": \"Spark\",  \"value\": 95, \"display\": \"95 / 100\" },\n    { \"label\": \"Flink\",  \"value\": 80 },\n    { \"label\": \"Trino\",  \"value\": 75 }\n  ]\n}"
        },
        {
          "kind": "bar-chart",
          "rows": [
            {
              "label": "Spark",
              "value": 95,
              "display": "95 / 100"
            },
            {
              "label": "Flink",
              "value": 80,
              "display": "80 / 100"
            },
            {
              "label": "Trino",
              "value": 75,
              "display": "75 / 100"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "heading",
          "level": 3,
          "id": "chart",
          "title": "chart"
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            "Generic SVG chart. ",
            {
              "kind": "code",
              "text": "type"
            },
            " is ",
            {
              "kind": "code",
              "text": "scatter"
            },
            " or ",
            {
              "kind": "code",
              "text": "line"
            },
            ". Series of points with optional per-point labels and per-series colors. Auto-scaled axes with 5 ticks each."
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "code",
          "language": "json",
          "source": "{\n  \"kind\": \"chart\",\n  \"type\": \"scatter\",\n  \"title\": \"Cost vs. impact\",\n  \"x_label\": \"Engineering cost\",\n  \"y_label\": \"User impact\",\n  \"series\": [\n    { \"label\": \"Sample series\", \"color\": \"accent\", \"data\": [\n      { \"x\": 4, \"y\": 9, \"label\": \"H3\" },\n      { \"x\": 6, \"y\": 8, \"label\": \"S2-inline\" }\n    ]}\n  ]\n}"
        },
        {
          "kind": "chart",
          "type": "scatter",
          "title": "Chart sample — cost vs. impact",
          "x_label": "Engineering cost",
          "y_label": "User impact",
          "series": [
            {
              "label": "Showstoppers + High",
              "color": "accent",
              "data": [
                {
                  "x": 4,
                  "y": 9,
                  "label": "H3"
                },
                {
                  "x": 6,
                  "y": 8,
                  "label": "S2-inline"
                },
                {
                  "x": 2,
                  "y": 5,
                  "label": "schema-validate"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "label": "Polish",
              "color": "warn",
              "data": [
                {
                  "x": 1,
                  "y": 2,
                  "label": "L1"
                },
                {
                  "x": 1,
                  "y": 3,
                  "label": "L3"
                },
                {
                  "x": 1,
                  "y": 2,
                  "label": "isTouch"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "heading",
          "level": 3,
          "id": "diagram",
          "title": "diagram"
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            "Mermaid-rendered. Lazy-loads Mermaid 10 from the CDN on first ",
            {
              "kind": "code",
              "text": "<diagram>"
            },
            " encountered on the page. ",
            {
              "kind": "code",
              "text": "source"
            },
            " is any Mermaid syntax (flowchart, sequence, gantt, state, class). Re-renders on theme toggle so colors track light/dark."
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "code",
          "language": "json",
          "source": "{\n  \"kind\": \"diagram\",\n  \"caption\": \"Optional caption below the diagram.\",\n  \"source\": \"flowchart LR\\n  A[JSON page] --> B(renderer)\\n  B --> C[DOM]\"\n}"
        },
        {
          "kind": "diagram",
          "caption": "Build pipeline at a glance.",
          "source": "flowchart LR\n    JSON[*.json pages] --> RJ[renderer.js]\n    RJ --> DOM[Custom Element DOM]\n    KIT[kit.json + glossary] --> CJ[chrome.js]\n    CJ --> DOM"
        },
        {
          "kind": "heading",
          "level": 3,
          "id": "live-snippet",
          "title": "live-snippet"
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            "Editable HTML/CSS/JS with sandboxed iframe preview. 220ms debounce on input. ",
            {
              "kind": "code",
              "text": "language"
            },
            " is currently ",
            {
              "kind": "code",
              "text": "html-css-js"
            },
            " (the only v1 mode). The Reset button restores the original ",
            {
              "kind": "code",
              "text": "source"
            },
            "."
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "code",
          "language": "json",
          "source": "{\n  \"kind\": \"live-snippet\",\n  \"label\": \"Edit the gradient and message\",\n  \"source\": \"<style>...</style>\\n<div>...</div>\"\n}"
        },
        {
          "kind": "live-snippet",
          "label": "Edit the markup — preview updates live",
          "source": "<style>\n  body { margin:0; height:100vh; display:grid; place-items:center;\n         background: linear-gradient(135deg, #115e59, #2dd4bf);\n         font-family: system-ui; }\n  .box { background:white; padding:20px 28px; border-radius:12px;\n         box-shadow:0 8px 24px rgba(0,0,0,0.15); }\n  h1 { margin:0 0 6px; color:#0f766e; font-size:20px; }\n  p  { margin:0; color:#475569; font-size:14px; }\n</style>\n<div class=\"box\">\n  <h1>Try the snippet</h1>\n  <p>Edit the source on the left.</p>\n</div>"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "section",
      "id": "layout-chrome",
      "title": "Layout / chrome — not in the page JSON",
      "lead": "page-chrome, page-nav, page-toc are set in the HTML stub, not the page JSON. The stub copy-pastes from templates/starter.html and you usually don't touch it.",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "code",
          "language": "html",
          "source": "<page-chrome></page-chrome>\n\n<div class=\"layout\">\n  <page-nav title=\"Pages\"></page-nav>\n  <main id=\"main-content\"></main>\n  <page-toc title=\"On this page\"></page-toc>\n</div>\n\n<script>\n  window.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', function () {\n    HtmlDocRenderer.autoBoot();\n  });\n</script>"
        },
        {
          "kind": "list",
          "style": "bullet",
          "items": [
            [
              {
                "kind": "code",
                "text": "<page-chrome>"
              },
              " — system cluster top-right (search, warning, theme cycler). Edge tabs for sidebars. Visual Viewport pinch-zoom tracker."
            ],
            [
              {
                "kind": "code",
                "text": "<page-nav>"
              },
              " — left site-tree sidebar. Reads site-manifest.json. Mark active page; edge-tab toggle."
            ],
            [
              {
                "kind": "code",
                "text": "<page-toc>"
              },
              " — right section-TOC sidebar. Built from main > section > h2/h3 after the renderer fires html-doc:rendered."
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "info-tip",
          "summary": "Customizing the layout",
          "content": [
            {
              "kind": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                "The kit defaults work for ~all KB pages. For one-off pages (a single-page artifact, no nav), drop the ",
                {
                  "kind": "code",
                  "text": "<page-nav>"
                },
                " element from the stub. Without it the layout falls back to two-column (TOC on left, like v1). The renderer doesn't care; it only owns ",
                {
                  "kind": "code",
                  "text": "<main>"
                },
                "."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "section",
      "id": "cross-cutting",
      "title": "Cross-cutting features",
      "lead": "Behaviors that don't introduce a new block kind but change how an existing one renders.",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "heading",
          "level": 3,
          "id": "ext-ref-cards",
          "title": "Citation cards via ext-ref"
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "content": "Existing <code>ext-ref</code> entries auto-promote to type-themed citation cards (paper / rfc / release / blog / other). Type is read from the extref entry or inferred from the link domain. Inline cite text inherits the type's color on its dotted underline; the hover card carries a type-tinted icon, a mono domain pill, optional author + date row, and a summary."
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            "Inline sample — hover any reference to see the card: see ",
            { "kind": "ext-ref", "name": "Iceberg paper" },
            " for the original snapshot-isolation argument, ",
            { "kind": "ext-ref", "name": "RFC 9457" },
            " for the HTTP problem-details format, and the ",
            { "kind": "ext-ref", "name": "Iceberg 1.4 release" },
            " for cross-engine sort orders."
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "heading",
          "level": 3,
          "id": "data-bind",
          "title": "Synced hover pairs · [data-bind]"
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "content": "Add <code>bind: \"step-3\"</code> to any two blocks and they flash together when either is hovered or focused. Click one — the offscreen partner scrolls into view. One-line opt-in per pair; no kind change required."
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "bind": "demo-bind",
          "content": "Inline sample — hover or focus this paragraph and the callout below tints in sync. They share the same data-bind key."
        },
        {
          "kind": "callout",
          "type": "tip",
          "bind": "demo-bind",
          "title": "Paired callout",
          "content": "Hovering the paragraph above lights this callout's border. Hovering this callout lights the paragraph. Same key, both directions."
        },
        {
          "kind": "heading",
          "level": 3,
          "id": "meta-updated",
          "title": "Last-updated line"
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "content": "<code>meta.updated</code> renders as a quiet italic line under the cover meta row. Pure trust signal — readers learn at a glance how fresh a page is."
        },
        {
          "kind": "code",
          "language": "json",
          "source": "{\n  \"kind\": \"page\",\n  \"title\": \"My note\",\n  \"meta\": {\n    \"date\": \"2026-05-10\",\n    \"updated\": \"2026-05-18\",\n    \"read_time\": \"~3 min\"\n  },\n  \"blocks\": [ ... ]\n}"
        },
        {
          "kind": "heading",
          "level": 3,
          "id": "admonition-aliases",
          "title": "Admonition vocab aliases"
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "content": "Callout <code>type</code> accepts both the kit's original names (<code>warn / warning / danger / success / neutral</code>) and the industry-standard aliases (<code>note / tip / info / caution</code>). Each row below is the same canonical styling reached from two different vocabularies."
        },
        {
          "kind": "callout",
          "type": "note",
          "title": "note · alias of neutral",
          "content": "<code>type: \"note\"</code> reads the same as <code>type: \"neutral\"</code> — generic informational tint."
        },
        {
          "kind": "callout",
          "type": "tip",
          "title": "tip · alias of success",
          "content": "<code>type: \"tip\"</code> matches <code>type: \"success\"</code> — green guidance accent for positive advice."
        },
        {
          "kind": "callout",
          "type": "info",
          "title": "info · alias of neutral with informational tint",
          "content": "Same surface as neutral; reserved name keeps Docusaurus / Mintlify habits intact."
        },
        {
          "kind": "callout",
          "type": "caution",
          "title": "caution · alias of warning",
          "content": "Amber border + icon; same look as <code>type: \"warning\"</code> from earlier rounds."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
